repository-code: 'https://github.com/morrocwi/zero-readout-certifies'
abstract: >-
  Arithmetic supplies the symbol 0; it does not say what a
  measurement returning that symbol has established. For the
  retained-information operator on a positively weighted
  comparison graph, the zero locus is shown to coincide, in
  both directions, with the locus at which no difference is
  retained across the declared structure — equivalently, with
  the fields constant on each connected component. The
  characterisation is machine-checked in Coq over the
  rationals without classical axioms. The paper argues that a
  zero readout is therefore not an absence but a
  classification, relative to the declared structure of
  comparison, and distinguishes it from an unresolved
  reading.
keywords:
  - zero
  - retained difference
  - graph Laplacian
  - Dirichlet energy
  - equivalence class
  - formal verification
  - Coq
  - philosophy of mathematics
